        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+3+2\\sqrt3)(x+3-2\\sqrt3)$\n\nComplete the square, then use the difference of two squares.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+6x-3&=(x^2+6x+9)-9-3\\\\x^2+6x-3&=(x+3)^2-12\\\\x^2+6x-3&=(x+3)^2-(2\\sqrt3)^2\\\\x^2+6x-3&=(x+3+2\\sqrt3)(x+3-2\\sqrt3)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-e15e-q3-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$x^2-10x-3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-5+2\\sqrt7)(x-5-2\\sqrt7)$\n\nComplete the square, then use the difference of two squares.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-10x-3&=(x^2-10x+25)-25-3\\\\x^2-10x-3&=(x-5)^2-28\\\\x^2-10x-3&=(x-5)^2-(2\\sqrt7)^2\\\\x^2-10x-3&=(x-5+2\\sqrt7)(x-5-2\\sqrt7)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
