        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+6+\\sqrt{41})(x+6-\\sqrt{41})$\n\nComplete the square, then use the difference of two squares.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+12x-5&=(x^2+12x+36)-36-5\\\\x^2+12x-5&=(x+6)^2-41\\\\x^2+12x-5&=(x+6)^2-(\\sqrt{41})^2\\\\x^2+12x-5&=(x+6+\\sqrt{41})(x+6-\\sqrt{41})\\end{align*}$$",
