        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(x+\\frac{9+\\sqrt{113}}2\\right)\\left(x+\\frac{9-\\sqrt{113}}2\\right)$\n\nComplete the square, then use the difference of two squares.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2+9x-8&=\\left(x^2+9x+\\frac{81}{4}\\right)-\\frac{81}{4}-8\\\\x^2+9x-8&=\\left(x+\\frac92\\right)^2-\\frac{113}{4}\\\\x^2+9x-8&=\\left(x+\\frac92\\right)^2-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{113}}2\\right)^2\\\\x^2+9x-8&=\\left(x+\\frac{9+\\sqrt{113}}2\\right)\\left(x+\\frac{9-\\sqrt{113}}2\\right)\\end{align*}$$",
