          "short": "$\\left(x-\\frac{7+\\sqrt{41}}2\\right)\\left(x-\\frac{7-\\sqrt{41}}2\\right)$\n\nComplete the square, then use the difference of two squares.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-7x+2&=\\left(x^2-7x+\\frac{49}{4}\\right)-\\frac{49}{4}+2\\\\x^2-7x+2&=\\left(x-\\frac72\\right)^2-\\frac{41}{4}\\\\x^2-7x+2&=\\left(x-\\frac72\\right)^2-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{41}}2\\right)^2\\\\x^2-7x+2&=\\left(x-\\frac{7+\\sqrt{41}}2\\right)\\left(x-\\frac{7-\\sqrt{41}}2\\right)\\end{align*}$$",
